# Python virtualenvs, wherever they are made. `venv` writes a `.gitignore`
# holding `*` inside the directory it creates, so git never sees these —
# prettier reads this file and nothing else, and without the line
# `npm run format:check` fails on nine LICENSE, SBOM and CSS files belonging to
# installed packages. CI checks out a clean tree and never saw them, so the
# check passed there and failed here. A check that only ever fails on noise is
# one people stop reading, which is how the format break in #143 reached main.
**/.venv*/
**/venv/
